---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "~/data/site";
const updated = "5 September 2026";
---
<Base
  title="Terms of service | MyWebMaster"
  description="The terms on which MyWebMaster provides Autopilot: what we do, what we do not change, ownership of work, the guarantee, cancellation and limits of liability."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Terms", href: "/legal/terms/" }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow prose">
      <p class="label">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of service</h1>
      <p class="mono muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <h2>1. What we provide</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} provides {site.product}, a subscription service that monitors a website,
        makes defined categories of change to it, and reports on the result. The categories of
        change permitted at each tier are published at
        <a href="/what-it-changes/">what it changes</a> and form part of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we will never change</h2>
      <p>
        We will not make automated changes to prices, guarantees, legal text, factual claims
        about your business, or indexing directives including <code>robots.txt</code>,
        <code>noindex</code>, canonical tags and hreflang. This limit applies at every tier and
        cannot be waived by agreement, because it exists to protect both parties.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Access and control</h2>
      <p>
        You grant us access to the repository and deployment pipeline for your site, and to your
        Search Console and analytics properties in a read-only capacity where possible. You may
        revoke that access at any time. A kill switch is available to you that halts all
        autonomous activity immediately.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        All work product — code, content, configuration and change history — belongs to you from
        the moment it is created. Nothing we produce is licensed back to you, and nothing is held
        in a system you cannot access after cancellation.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Measurement and the guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        On the Compound tier, results are measured by comparing optimised pages against a control
        group over a fixed window. If the control group outperforms the treatment group across
        two consecutive measurement windows, the fee for the second of those months is refunded.
        The guarantee applies to the measured comparison only and does not extend to absolute
        traffic or revenue outcomes.
      </p>

      <h2>6. What we cannot promise</h2>
      <p>
        Search rankings are determined by third parties whose systems we do not control. We do
        not promise specific positions, traffic volumes or revenue, and any provider who does is
        promising something they cannot deliver. We promise method, transparency and measurement.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Cancellation</h2>
      <p>
        Watch and Apply may be cancelled at any time, effective at the end of the current billing
        month. Compound has a three-month minimum term because a holdout comparison requires a
        full measurement window plus a readout to produce a meaningful result.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Our total liability in connection with the service is limited to the fees paid in the
        three months preceding the event giving rise to the claim. Nothing in these terms limits
        liability for death, personal injury, or fraud. Because every change is version
        controlled and reversible, our first remedy for any error is to revert it.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { margin-block: 1rem 0.5rem; }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 2.2em; font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .prose a { color: var(--accent); }
  code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.88em; background: var(--bg-soft); padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 3px; }
</style>
